{"term":"plump","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:ba91c8b93953f39da0","definition":"Having a full and rounded shape; chubby, somewhat overweight.","example":"a plump baby; plump cheeks","pos":"adj","synonyms":["round"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:446c5828a2d4afa151","definition":"Sudden and without reservation; blunt; direct; downright.","example":"We are averse to plump queries, but we are going to ask our readers a plain, simple question Did you ever see a paper y'clept \"The Yankee Blade?\"","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:66f0390bbe5b5bf088","definition":"Of a wine: giving the sensation of filling the mouth.","example":"A plump wine, with an abundance of plum and berry characteristics and soft, round tannins. Easy to drink; ready on release.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:14327d80008aee4c45","definition":"To grow plump; to swell out.","example":"Her cheeks have plumped.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump","plump for","plump up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:569f4c0872305f8a40","definition":"To make plump; to fill (out) or support; often with up.","example":"to plump oysters or scallops by placing them in fresh or brackish water","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump","plump for","plump up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9bf564192c546e9552","definition":"To give a plumper (kind of vote).","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump","plump for","plump up"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:fdf5107f1c561b5da6","definition":"To give (a vote), as a plumper.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitud