","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump","plump for","plump up","plump down"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:de80e68c7857f812d8","definition":"Directly; suddenly; perpendicularly.","example":"I suppose then, that going plump on a flying whale with your sail set in a foggy squall is the height of a whaleman’s discretion?","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump","plump for","plump up","plump down"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b7806b685be5600aee","definition":"The sound of a sudden heavy fall.","example":"As she beheld her, poor Mrs. Mack's heart fluttered up to her mouth, and then dropped with a dreadful plump, into the pit of her stomach.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie","plumping","plumpish","plumpitude","plumpkin","plumply","plumpness","plumptious","plumptitude","plumpy","unplump","plump for","plump up","plump down"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plump#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0aad7863fac83ec058","definition":"A knot or cluster; a group; a crowd.","example":"a plump of trees, fowls, or spears","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["overplump","plumpage","plumpie"